  "body": "Reworded the user-visible refusals that said \"furniture\" (our in-code word) so they name what the thing is. Same conditions refuse, same commands, nothing posted changes, no snapshot PNG, MCP tool names and schemas untouched.\n\n## Review round (head 59c4b955)\nThe first \"not a model\" sentence said \"part of a setup (its stock, work offset or fixtures)\". That branch fires whenever `model::is_model` is false, which also covers tools, operations, setups and program entries, so it was false for them. Fixtures never reach the branch. The sentence now matches the condition.\n\n## Strings before -> after\n| File | Line | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `crates/app/src/commands/repair_model.rs` | 47 | `'{name}' is setup furniture, not a model` | `'{name}' is not a model - it is a setup's stock or work offset, a setup, a tool, an operation or other CAM data` |\n| `crates/app/src/commands/update_model.rs` | 81 | `'{name}' is setup furniture, not a model` | same as above |\n| `crates/app/src/commands/fixture.rs` | 91 | `'{name}' is the setup's stock, work offset or CAM data, not a model to mark` | `'{name}' is not a model, so it cannot be marked as a fixture - it is a setup's stock or work offset, a setup, a tool, an operation or other CAM data` (same `is_model` condition, aligned) |\n| `crates/app/src/commands/setup.rs` | 95 | `a setup name must not contain '/' - that separator belongs to setup furniture` | `a setup name must not contain '/' - names with '/' are reserved for a setup's own stock and work offset` |\n| `crates/app/src/commands/setup.rs` | 109 | `'{name}' is reserved for setup furniture` | `'{name}' is a name reserved for a setup's stock and work offsets` |\n| `crates/app/src/commands/tool.rs` | 32 | `'{name}' is reserved for setup furniture` | same as setup.rs:109 |\n\n## Search (crates/*/src, case-insensitive, literals only)\n- Changed: the literals above. Nothing in `crates/app/src/mcp/` or `crates/app/src/script/` (hits are comments only).\n- `project/validate.rs:122` already plain: left.\n- Comments, identifiers (`is_furniture_*`), `//!` headers and ui code comments: left. Ui assertion messages in `tests.rs` and `law_tests.rs`: left.\n\n## Tests\n- `crates/app/tests/repair_model.rs`: the existing refusal test now expects \"is not a model\" and checks no \"furniture\".\n- New `tools_and_operations_are_refused_as_not_models_not_setup_parts`: a tool (`EM-0400-2FL`) and an operation (`Face1`) through `RepairModel::new` and `UpdateModel::new`; each refusal must contain \"is not a model\", must not contain \"part of a setup\", and must not contain \"furniture\".\n- Guard `setup_refusals_never_say_furniture` in `crates/app/tests/setups.rs` (unchanged).\n- `docs/decisions/878-furniture-plain-refusals.md` updated to the corrected wording.\n\n## Run (head 59c4b955)\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test repair_model`: 5 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test setups`: 12 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test commands_undo -- update_validates_at_construction`: 1 passed (no dedicated update-model binary exists; this covers UpdateModel's construction refusals).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The `cargo xtask gate quick` run from the first round was not repeated on this head; the three binaries above were run directly. The TagFixture refusal's text has no test pinning it, and it was not run through a test.\n- The ui crate was not built (no ui string changed).\n\nChangelog: none (user-visible wording only; no behaviour change).\n\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #878\n",
